{0 Bincaml IR Language server }

This is a language server for the {{: https://github.com/agle/bincaml } Bincaml}
intermediate language. These files usually have the [.il] file extension.

It provides the following basic functionality:

- go to definition of block/global/parameter variables, blocks, procedures, ADT cases, and declared type names.
- hover information of the above terms,
- autocompletion of the above terms,
- symbol tree view,
- procedure DOT graph generation,
- syntax error highlighting from lexer / parser,
- loading error highlighting (e.g., due to undefined variable errors),
- debug highlight mode where every token is highlighted.

To use it, you should build or obtain the LSP executable, then set the path to
the binary as the LSP for the language associated with [.il] files.

{1 Installation}

To obtain the LSP executable, you can check out and build it (if doing this, it is
convenient to use a different folder to your usual copy).

It is also available
through the Nix flake, with [nix build .#bincaml_lsp -o bincaml-lsp], or within the Nix
dev shell, as [bincaml_lsp] inside [nix develop].

{1 Setup}

Finally, it can be configured in Astronvim with this inside your [astrolsp.lua]:

{[
    servers = {
       "basillsp"
    },
    config = {
      basillsp = {
        cmd={".../_build/default/lsp/bin/main.exe"}, filetypes={"basilir"}, root_dir = require("lspconfig.util").root_pattern("."),
      },
    },
]}

For Helix, see {{: https://docs.helix-editor.com/languages.html#language-server-configuration} Language Server configuration}.


{1 Modules}

- {!module:Bincaml_lsp}

